summary:

In this post, I take lessons from Lauren Tan's AI Engineer CODE 2026 talk on verifying coding agents (deterministic checks, clean codebases, and reviewing evidence instead of code) and apply them to data science. I connect her ideas to project templates, Pandera schemas, and artifact-based review, then argue data science must go one step further: asking whether results are correct, defensible, and independently supported. When agents make verification this cheap, what's stopping us from building it into every analysis?
---
